        ['id'=>9360,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2761,'title'=>'International Observers Question Legitimacy of 301 Vote Count','exc'=>'The count continued through the night as the margin between the leading candidates proved too narrow for any party to claim a mandate before all ballots had been verified.','body'=>'<p>When the full account is eventually written, historians will note the particular quality of the moment: the sense among those living through it that something significant was happening, combined with an inability to be certain about precisely what it meant.</p><p>Contemporaries who tried to find precedents for comparison found them only partially useful, because while the surface resemblances were real, the underlying conditions were different enough to make analogies more misleading than illuminating.</p><p>What was not in doubt was that the event had accelerated timelines and concentrated minds in ways that incrementalism alone would not have achieved in the same period.</p><p>The challenge now was to convert that concentrated attention into durable commitments, a challenge that history suggested was substantially harder than the moments of acute focus that preceded it might imply.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'James Carver','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540910419892-4a36d2c3266c?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Election','Democracy','Vote'],'date'=>'2022-11-14 17:48:00'],
