        ['id'=>9364,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>4210,'title'=>'twelve% of Gaza Buildings Damaged, Satellite Analysis Reveals','exc'=>'Medical workers described desperate conditions as supplies ran critically low for the third consecutive week, with the last functioning generator at risk of shutdown.','body'=>'<p>The situation developed with a speed that left observers struggling to keep pace, as each new development built on the last in ways that underscored the interconnected nature of the forces at work.</p><p>Those with deep expertise in the area described it as a confluence of trends that had each been building independently for years before arriving simultaneously at a point of acute pressure.</p><p>The institutional response was measured, with officials taking care to frame their position in a way that acknowledged the complexity without appearing to minimise the significance of what was unfolding.</p><p>What comes next remains genuinely uncertain, though the structural conditions that produced the current moment show no sign of resolving themselves quickly or easily.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Sophie Laurent','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1526374965328-7f61d4dc18c5?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Israel','War','UN'],'date'=>'2024-07-24 07:47:00'],
