        ['id'=>9471,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1601,'title'=>'Coral Bleaching Event Declared Across 4 Percent of Great Barrier Reef','exc'=>'Emergency services were overwhelmed as the disaster unfolded far more rapidly than forecasters had projected, with the scale of human displacement exceeding the capacity of existing relief structures.','body'=>'<p>Numbers can capture the scale of what occurred but not its texture. Behind the figures were individual stories that defied easy summary and that the official account, necessarily schematic, was unable to convey.</p><p>Researchers who had spent years tracking the subject described a mix of vindication and alarm at how events had unfolded, saying the data had long pointed in this direction but that the pace was faster than even pessimistic scenarios had suggested.</p><p>The policy response drew criticism from those who argued it was too slow, too limited, and too deferential to interests that had contributed to the situation rather than helping to prevent it.</p><p>Future analysis will inevitably focus on the decisions not taken in the years before, and on whether different choices at key junctures would have led to materially different outcomes.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Priya Nair','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1532094349884-543282300eed?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Climate','Emissions','COP'],'date'=>'2024-10-02 08:31:00'],
        ['id'=>9472,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1848,'title'=>'AI-Generated Deepfakes Flood unprecedented Electoral Campaign in Final Days','exc'=>'Political scientists said the result reflected a broader pattern of incumbent parties struggling to hold their coalitions together as the cost of living continued to dominate voter concern.','body'=>'<p>When the full account is eventually written, historians will note the particular quality of the moment: the sense among those living through it that something significant was happening, combined with an inability to be certain about precisely what it meant.</p><p>Contemporaries who tried to find precedents for comparison found them only partially useful, because while the surface resemblances were real, the underlying conditions were different enough to make analogies more misleading than illuminating.</p><p>What was not in doubt was that the event had accelerated timelines and concentrated minds in ways that incrementalism alone would not have achieved in the same period.</p><p>The challenge now was to convert that concentrated attention into durable commitments, a challenge that history suggested was substantially harder than the moments of acute focus that preceded it might imply.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Elena Vasquez','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540910419892-4a36d2c3266c?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Election','Democracy','Vote'],'date'=>'2022-11-22 14:52:00'],
        ['id'=>9473,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>946,'title'=>'Integration Crisis: 58 Says Infrastructure Cannot Absorb Arrivals','exc'=>'The legal challenge centred on whether the policy complied with international obligations that the government argued had been superseded by the scale of the pressure it was facing.','body'=>'<p>The situation developed with a speed that left observers struggling to keep pace, as each new development built on the last in ways that underscored the interconnected nature of the forces at work.</p><p>Those with deep expertise in the area described it as a confluence of trends that had each been building independently for years before arriving simultaneously at a point of acute pressure.</p><p>The institutional response was measured, with officials taking care to frame their position in a way that acknowledged the complexity without appearing to minimise the significance of what was unfolding.</p><p>What comes next remains genuinely uncertain, though the structural conditions that produced the current moment show no sign of resolving themselves quickly or easily.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Ahmed Al-Rashid','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495020689067-958852172e31?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Migration','Refugees','Border'],'date'=>'2024-10-01 22:50:00'],
