        ['id'=>9515,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>199,'title'=>'53% of serious Population Under 25 Drives Consumer Market Surge','exc'=>'Economists pointed to diversification away from commodity dependence as the structural change underpinning the strong numbers, cautioning that the trajectory remained vulnerable to external shocks.','body'=>'<p>The situation developed with a speed that left observers struggling to keep pace, as each new development built on the last in ways that underscored the interconnected nature of the forces at work.</p><p>Those with deep expertise in the area described it as a confluence of trends that had each been building independently for years before arriving simultaneously at a point of acute pressure.</p><p>The institutional response was measured, with officials taking care to frame their position in a way that acknowledged the complexity without appearing to minimise the significance of what was unfolding.</p><p>What comes next remains genuinely uncertain, though the structural conditions that produced the current moment show no sign of resolving themselves quickly or easily.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Marcus Webb','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1588681664899-f142ff2dc9b1?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Sahel','Security','Conflict'],'date'=>'2024-05-13 08:58:00'],
        ['id'=>9516,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>370,'title'=>'Two-State Solution Discussions Revived by a hundred and fifty Nations','exc'=>'Diplomats at the United Nations said the stalemate reflected fundamental divisions among permanent members that made binding collective action effectively impossible.','body'=>'<p>Numbers can capture the scale of what occurred but not its texture. Behind the figures were individual stories that defied easy summary and that the official account, necessarily schematic, was unable to convey.</p><p>Researchers who had spent years tracking the subject described a mix of vindication and alarm at how events had unfolded, saying the data had long pointed in this direction but that the pace was faster than even pessimistic scenarios had suggested.</p><p>The policy response drew criticism from those who argued it was too slow, too limited, and too deferential to interests that had contributed to the situation rather than helping to prevent it.</p><p>Future analysis will inevitably focus on the decisions not taken in the years before, and on whether different choices at key junctures would have led to materially different outcomes.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Fatima Hussain','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1526374965328-7f61d4dc18c5?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Ceasefire','Diplomacy','Gaza'],'date'=>'2023-09-11 10:26:00'],
