        ['id'=>9518,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>3261,'title'=>'Taiwan Presidential Election Result Rejects Pro-Beijing Candidate','exc'=>'The vote was widely seen as a referendum on the island\'s relationship with mainland China, with the result interpreted internationally as a clear signal from the population.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Liu Wei','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1569025591579-dc1e22e82e14?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Semiconductors','Trade','Geopolitics'],'date'=>'2024-07-03 07:00:00'],
