        ['id'=>9547,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>193,'title'=>'Coup in seven: Military Junta Seizes Power and Suspends Constitution','exc'=>'Debt sustainability advocates said the terms of several large infrastructure loans would leave the government with obligations that would constrain public spending for a generation.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Daniel Osei','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1588681664899-f142ff2dc9b1?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Debt','China','Trade'],'date'=>'2023-05-04 09:58:00'],
        ['id'=>9548,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1234,'title'=>'UN Security Council Fails to Pass Gaza Ceasefire Resolution for 82 Time','exc'=>'Journalists on the ground reported scenes of mass displacement, with families carrying what possessions they could as evacuation orders covered an expanding area.','body'=>'<p>Few events arrive fully formed. The roots of this one stretched back further than most accounts acknowledged, through a series of decisions, deferred choices, and accumulated pressures that had been visible to specialists for years.</p><p>The immediate trigger was real enough, but veterans of the subject said it should be understood as the proximate rather than the underlying cause of a development that had, in retrospect, an air of inevitability.</p><p>Institutions moved to respond, though the speed and coherence of that response drew mixed assessments from outside observers who questioned whether the frameworks in place were suited to what they were now being asked to manage.</p><p>The longer-term significance will be debated for years, but the immediate effect was to reshape the landscape in ways that all parties involved will need to navigate carefully if the situation is to stabilise.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Liu Wei','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1526374965328-7f61d4dc18c5?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Humanitarian','Aid','Crisis'],'date'=>'2022-06-09 16:56:00'],
