        ['id'=>9588,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2978,'title'=>'Egypt Warns of Regional Escalation as Gaza Death Toll Mounts','exc'=>'Journalists on the ground reported scenes of mass displacement, with families carrying what possessions they could as evacuation orders covered an expanding area.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Liu Wei','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1526374965328-7f61d4dc18c5?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Israel','War','UN'],'date'=>'2024-07-15 19:18:00'],
