        ['id'=>9607,'published'=>true,'featured'=>true,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1915,'title'=>'Permafrost Thaw Releasing Methane at Rate Beyond Model Predictions','exc'=>'Negotiators emerged from the final session with an agreement that environmental campaigners immediately condemned as wholly inadequate to the speed and scale of the changes already under way.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Daniel Osei','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1532094349884-543282300eed?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Wildfire','Heat','Extreme Weather'],'date'=>'2022-04-22 12:15:00'],
