        ['id'=>9752,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1367,'title'=>'Social Media Blackout Ordered During historic Election Day Polling','exc'=>'The winning candidate struck a conciliatory tone in a victory speech that nonetheless signalled a sharp change in direction from the policies of the outgoing administration.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'World News','author'=>'Elena Vasquez','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540910419892-4a36d2c3266c?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Election','Democracy','Vote'],'date'=>'2022-03-09 15:24:00'],
