        ['id'=>10054,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>3072,'title'=>'Office Space Disposal: sweeping Exits 345 Billion in Commercial Leases','exc'=>'Investors welcomed the announcement, seeing in it an acknowledgement that the previous management\'s strategy had failed to deliver the returns that the asset base warranted.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Claire Dupont','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1565728744382-61accd811aa9?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Private Equity','Buyout','Investment'],'date'=>'2023-10-17 09:48:00'],
