        ['id'=>10074,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>944,'title'=>'OpenAI Revenue Reaches ten Billion Annualised, Seeks New Funding','exc'=>'The figures reinforced the view that cloud computing and artificial intelligence services had become the primary drivers of financial performance in the technology sector.','body'=>'<p>When the full account is eventually written, historians will note the particular quality of the moment: the sense among those living through it that something significant was happening, combined with an inability to be certain about precisely what it meant.</p><p>Contemporaries who tried to find precedents for comparison found them only partially useful, because while the surface resemblances were real, the underlying conditions were different enough to make analogies more misleading than illuminating.</p><p>What was not in doubt was that the event had accelerated timelines and concentrated minds in ways that incrementalism alone would not have achieved in the same period.</p><p>The challenge now was to convert that concentrated attention into durable commitments, a challenge that history suggested was substantially harder than the moments of acute focus that preceded it might imply.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Claire Dupont','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1554224155-6726b3ff858f?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Earnings','Revenue','Profit'],'date'=>'2022-12-19 16:23:00'],
        ['id'=>10075,'published'=>true,'featured'=>true,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>918,'title'=>'BNPL Lenders Face Crackdown as serious Percent of Users Miss Payments','exc'=>'The collapse unfolded with stunning speed, shaking confidence in institutions that regulators had repeatedly described as systemically sound and adequately capitalised.','body'=>'<p>Numbers can capture the scale of what occurred but not its texture. Behind the figures were individual stories that defied easy summary and that the official account, necessarily schematic, was unable to convey.</p><p>Researchers who had spent years tracking the subject described a mix of vindication and alarm at how events had unfolded, saying the data had long pointed in this direction but that the pace was faster than even pessimistic scenarios had suggested.</p><p>The policy response drew criticism from those who argued it was too slow, too limited, and too deferential to interests that had contributed to the situation rather than helping to prevent it.</p><p>Future analysis will inevitably focus on the decisions not taken in the years before, and on whether different choices at key junctures would have led to materially different outcomes.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Noah Okafor','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507003211169-0a1dd7228f2d?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Finance','IMF','Debt'],'date'=>'2022-11-11 13:35:00'],
        ['id'=>10076,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2159,'title'=>'Carbon Credit Market Hits 103 Billion as Corporates Offset Emissions','exc'=>'The investment decision signalled a strategic retreat from commitments made under heavy investor and regulatory pressure, returning the company to a production-first orientation.','body'=>'<p>Few events arrive fully formed. The roots of this one stretched back further than most accounts acknowledged, through a series of decisions, deferred choices, and accumulated pressures that had been visible to specialists for years.</p><p>The immediate trigger was real enough, but veterans of the subject said it should be understood as the proximate rather than the underlying cause of a development that had, in retrospect, an air of inevitability.</p><p>Institutions moved to respond, though the speed and coherence of that response drew mixed assessments from outside observers who questioned whether the frameworks in place were suited to what they were now being asked to manage.</p><p>The longer-term significance will be debated for years, but the immediate effect was to reshape the landscape in ways that all parties involved will need to navigate carefully if the situation is to stabilise.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Sarah Chen','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1460925895917-afdab827c52f?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Gas','LNG','Commodities'],'date'=>'2023-02-26 07:16:00'],
