        ['id'=>10139,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2775,'title'=>'Automation Threat: five% of 397 Jobs At High Risk Over Decade','exc'=>'Currency strategists described the pressure as a function of interest rate differentials that the affected central bank had limited tools to counter without imposing painful restrictions on credit.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Yuki Nakamura','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1611974789855-9c2a0a7236a3?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Poverty','Inequality','Development'],'date'=>'2025-07-21 21:53:00'],
