        ['id'=>10141,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>256,'title'=>'Shadow Banking Sector in China Nears sweeping Trillion in Total Liabilities','exc'=>'Economists said the figures highlighted an uncomfortable paradox, with financial sector profits rising at a time when the broader economy was showing signs of stress.','body'=>'<p>Numbers can capture the scale of what occurred but not its texture. Behind the figures were individual stories that defied easy summary and that the official account, necessarily schematic, was unable to convey.</p><p>Researchers who had spent years tracking the subject described a mix of vindication and alarm at how events had unfolded, saying the data had long pointed in this direction but that the pace was faster than even pessimistic scenarios had suggested.</p><p>The policy response drew criticism from those who argued it was too slow, too limited, and too deferential to interests that had contributed to the situation rather than helping to prevent it.</p><p>Future analysis will inevitably focus on the decisions not taken in the years before, and on whether different choices at key junctures would have led to materially different outcomes.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Oliver Grant','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507003211169-0a1dd7228f2d?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Investment','Bonds','Market'],'date'=>'2022-11-08 12:44:00'],
