        ['id'=>10189,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>4555,'title'=>'JPMorgan Profit Rises fifty% as Net Interest Income Hits Record','exc'=>'The move marked a significant policy shift that analysts said had been debated internally for months and reflected a fundamental reassessment of the balance between growth and stability.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Yuki Nakamura','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507003211169-0a1dd7228f2d?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Finance','IMF','Debt'],'date'=>'2023-07-08 15:19:00'],
