        ['id'=>10210,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2896,'title'=>'Activist Investor Takes 217% Stake in ten, Demands Board Changes','exc'=>'Regulators said the conditions they had placed on the transaction were non-negotiable and reflected genuine concerns about market concentration that the parties had not adequately addressed.','body'=>'<p>When the full account is eventually written, historians will note the particular quality of the moment: the sense among those living through it that something significant was happening, combined with an inability to be certain about precisely what it meant.</p><p>Contemporaries who tried to find precedents for comparison found them only partially useful, because while the surface resemblances were real, the underlying conditions were different enough to make analogies more misleading than illuminating.</p><p>What was not in doubt was that the event had accelerated timelines and concentrated minds in ways that incrementalism alone would not have achieved in the same period.</p><p>The challenge now was to convert that concentrated attention into durable commitments, a challenge that history suggested was substantially harder than the moments of acute focus that preceded it might imply.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Rachel Kim','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1565728744382-61accd811aa9?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Mergers','Acquisitions','Corporate'],'date'=>'2022-09-07 12:28:00'],
