        ['id'=>10251,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>4686,'title'=>'Critical Minerals Agreement Signed by three Nations Excluding China','exc'=>'The agreement represented years of painstaking negotiation and would, its architects said, create new opportunities particularly for smaller exporters that had previously lacked access to the larger market.','body'=>'<p>The situation developed with a speed that left observers struggling to keep pace, as each new development built on the last in ways that underscored the interconnected nature of the forces at work.</p><p>Those with deep expertise in the area described it as a confluence of trends that had each been building independently for years before arriving simultaneously at a point of acute pressure.</p><p>The institutional response was measured, with officials taking care to frame their position in a way that acknowledged the complexity without appearing to minimise the significance of what was unfolding.</p><p>What comes next remains genuinely uncertain, though the structural conditions that produced the current moment show no sign of resolving themselves quickly or easily.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Oliver Grant','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1486406146926-c627a92ad1ab?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Semiconductors','Manufacturing','Reshoring'],'date'=>'2024-12-17 18:19:00'],
