        ['id'=>10274,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>3666,'title'=>'LNG Terminal Opens in 128, Reducing Dependence on Russian Supplies','exc'=>'Analysts noted that the irony of record fossil fuel profits coinciding with the most prominent international climate meetings in years was not lost on campaigners or on the companies themselves.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Claire Dupont','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1460925895917-afdab827c52f?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Gas','LNG','Commodities'],'date'=>'2024-03-12 21:31:00'],
        ['id'=>10275,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>672,'title'=>'Global Shipping Costs Up 106% After Red Sea Crisis Deepens','exc'=>'Risk consultants described the concentration of production in a small number of facilities and regions as one of the most significant vulnerabilities in the global economic architecture.','body'=>'<p>Few events arrive fully formed. The roots of this one stretched back further than most accounts acknowledged, through a series of decisions, deferred choices, and accumulated pressures that had been visible to specialists for years.</p><p>The immediate trigger was real enough, but veterans of the subject said it should be understood as the proximate rather than the underlying cause of a development that had, in retrospect, an air of inevitability.</p><p>Institutions moved to respond, though the speed and coherence of that response drew mixed assessments from outside observers who questioned whether the frameworks in place were suited to what they were now being asked to manage.</p><p>The longer-term significance will be debated for years, but the immediate effect was to reshape the landscape in ways that all parties involved will need to navigate carefully if the situation is to stabilise.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Noah Okafor','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1486406146926-c627a92ad1ab?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Supply Chain','Logistics','Shipping'],'date'=>'2023-12-09 15:04:00'],
