        ['id'=>10282,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>124,'title'=>'two Merger Called Off as Regulators Demand Unacceptable Remedies','exc'=>'Corporate governance experts said the episode highlighted systemic weaknesses in how boards were composed and incentivised, arguing that more structural change was needed beyond individual accountability.','body'=>'<p>The situation developed with a speed that left observers struggling to keep pace, as each new development built on the last in ways that underscored the interconnected nature of the forces at work.</p><p>Those with deep expertise in the area described it as a confluence of trends that had each been building independently for years before arriving simultaneously at a point of acute pressure.</p><p>The institutional response was measured, with officials taking care to frame their position in a way that acknowledged the complexity without appearing to minimise the significance of what was unfolding.</p><p>What comes next remains genuinely uncertain, though the structural conditions that produced the current moment show no sign of resolving themselves quickly or easily.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Anjali Sharma','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1565728744382-61accd811aa9?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Private Equity','Buyout','Investment'],'date'=>'2022-05-29 19:52:00'],
