        ['id'=>10351,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>3886,'title'=>'Federal Reserve Holds Rates at dramatic% Amid Mixed Economic Signals','exc'=>'Central bankers said the decision reflected genuine uncertainty about the balance of risks and signalled that the path of future policy would be entirely dependent on incoming data.','body'=>'<p>Few events arrive fully formed. The roots of this one stretched back further than most accounts acknowledged, through a series of decisions, deferred choices, and accumulated pressures that had been visible to specialists for years.</p><p>The immediate trigger was real enough, but veterans of the subject said it should be understood as the proximate rather than the underlying cause of a development that had, in retrospect, an air of inevitability.</p><p>Institutions moved to respond, though the speed and coherence of that response drew mixed assessments from outside observers who questioned whether the frameworks in place were suited to what they were now being asked to manage.</p><p>The longer-term significance will be debated for years, but the immediate effect was to reshape the landscape in ways that all parties involved will need to navigate carefully if the situation is to stabilise.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Oliver Grant','img'=>'','tags'=>['Banking','Fed','Interest Rates'],'date'=>'2023-01-30 07:17:00'],
        ['id'=>10352,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>611,'title'=>'Oil Hits serious Dollars as OPEC+ Extends Production Cut by 445 Months','exc'=>'Traders said the price movement reflected genuine tightness in physical supply rather than speculative positioning, adding that the market was likely to remain volatile through the season.','body'=>'<p>When the full account is eventually written, historians will note the particular quality of the moment: the sense among those living through it that something significant was happening, combined with an inability to be certain about precisely what it meant.</p><p>Contemporaries who tried to find precedents for comparison found them only partially useful, because while the surface resemblances were real, the underlying conditions were different enough to make analogies more misleading than illuminating.</p><p>What was not in doubt was that the event had accelerated timelines and concentrated minds in ways that incrementalism alone would not have achieved in the same period.</p><p>The challenge now was to convert that concentrated attention into durable commitments, a challenge that history suggested was substantially harder than the moments of acute focus that preceded it might imply.</p>','cat'=>'Business','author'=>'Anjali Sharma','img'=>'','tags'=>['Oil','OPEC','Energy'],'date'=>'2024-01-06 05:07:00'],
