        ['id'=>10443,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>4909,'title'=>'Space Debris Crisis: twenty Near-Miss Events Reported This Year','exc'=>'Mission controllers described the moment as one that validated years of iteration, failure, and redesign, saying it opened the door to a cadence of flights that would have seemed implausible just years before.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Technology','author'=>'Diego Reyes','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504384308090-c894fdcc538d?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Satellite','Starlink','Internet'],'date'=>'2022-09-27 22:51:00'],
        ['id'=>10444,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>318,'title'=>'YouTube Shorts Surpasses twelve Billion Daily Views, Threatening TikTok','exc'=>'Platform executives described the policy change as a carefully balanced measure, while critics argued it prioritised engagement metrics over user wellbeing in ways that the internal research had long flagged.','body'=>'<p>Few events arrive fully formed. The roots of this one stretched back further than most accounts acknowledged, through a series of decisions, deferred choices, and accumulated pressures that had been visible to specialists for years.</p><p>The immediate trigger was real enough, but veterans of the subject said it should be understood as the proximate rather than the underlying cause of a development that had, in retrospect, an air of inevitability.</p><p>Institutions moved to respond, though the speed and coherence of that response drew mixed assessments from outside observers who questioned whether the frameworks in place were suited to what they were now being asked to manage.</p><p>The longer-term significance will be debated for years, but the immediate effect was to reshape the landscape in ways that all parties involved will need to navigate carefully if the situation is to stabilise.</p>','cat'=>'Technology','author'=>'Yuki Tanaka','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555949963-aa79dcee981c?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['EU','Regulation','DMA'],'date'=>'2025-07-27 08:34:00'],
        ['id'=>10445,'published'=>true,'featured'=>true,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>4184,'title'=>'Sam Altman Calls for Global AI Governance Body at two Summit','exc'=>'Researchers at institutions that had been sceptical of rapid capability gains acknowledged that the benchmark results represented a qualitative shift in what the technology could accomplish.','body'=>'<p>When the full account is eventually written, historians will note the particular quality of the moment: the sense among those living through it that something significant was happening, combined with an inability to be certain about precisely what it meant.</p><p>Contemporaries who tried to find precedents for comparison found them only partially useful, because while the surface resemblances were real, the underlying conditions were different enough to make analogies more misleading than illuminating.</p><p>What was not in doubt was that the event had accelerated timelines and concentrated minds in ways that incrementalism alone would not have achieved in the same period.</p><p>The challenge now was to convert that concentrated attention into durable commitments, a challenge that history suggested was substantially harder than the moments of acute focus that preceded it might imply.</p>','cat'=>'Technology','author'=>'Alex Porter','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['LLM','Model','Benchmark'],'date'=>'2023-10-18 14:19:00'],
