        ['id'=>10518,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>658,'title'=>'Space Debris Crisis: two Near-Miss Events Reported This Year','exc'=>'Scientists said the discovery warranted immediate follow-up observation, while stressing that any claim of biological origin would require a standard of evidence far beyond what a single spectroscopic measurement could provide.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Technology','author'=>'Priya Desai','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504384308090-c894fdcc538d?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Space','SpaceX','Rocket'],'date'=>'2022-03-16 20:38:00'],
