        ['id'=>10531,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2415,'title'=>'New Malware 189 Uses AI to Evade Detection for Average 195 Days','exc'=>'Officials declined to attribute the intrusion publicly but said privately that the characteristics were consistent with a known state-sponsored threat actor that had been tracked for years.','body'=>'<p>Few events arrive fully formed. The roots of this one stretched back further than most accounts acknowledged, through a series of decisions, deferred choices, and accumulated pressures that had been visible to specialists for years.</p><p>The immediate trigger was real enough, but veterans of the subject said it should be understood as the proximate rather than the underlying cause of a development that had, in retrospect, an air of inevitability.</p><p>Institutions moved to respond, though the speed and coherence of that response drew mixed assessments from outside observers who questioned whether the frameworks in place were suited to what they were now being asked to manage.</p><p>The longer-term significance will be debated for years, but the immediate effect was to reshape the landscape in ways that all parties involved will need to navigate carefully if the situation is to stabilise.</p>','cat'=>'Technology','author'=>'Ravi Patel','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1526374965328-7f61d4dc18c5?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Nation State','Espionage','Attack'],'date'=>'2024-10-27 19:53:00'],
        ['id'=>10532,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2629,'title'=>'Hydrogen Fuel Cell Trucks Begin Commercial Operation in 349','exc'=>'The milestone was described by advocates as the clearest signal yet that the transition away from internal combustion engines had reached a point of no return in the country\'s new vehicle market.','body'=>'<p>The situation developed with a speed that left observers struggling to keep pace, as each new development built on the last in ways that underscored the interconnected nature of the forces at work.</p><p>Those with deep expertise in the area described it as a confluence of trends that had each been building independently for years before arriving simultaneously at a point of acute pressure.</p><p>The institutional response was measured, with officials taking care to frame their position in a way that acknowledged the complexity without appearing to minimise the significance of what was unfolding.</p><p>What comes next remains genuinely uncertain, though the structural conditions that produced the current moment show no sign of resolving themselves quickly or easily.</p>','cat'=>'Technology','author'=>'Chloe Marsh','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1550751827-4bd374c3f58b?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['BYD','China','Automakers'],'date'=>'2022-02-09 08:27:00'],
        ['id'=>10533,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1173,'title'=>'Space Tourism Price Falls to 188 as Competition Between Providers Grows','exc'=>'Scientists said the discovery warranted immediate follow-up observation, while stressing that any claim of biological origin would require a standard of evidence far beyond what a single spectroscopic measurement could provide.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Technology','author'=>'Diego Reyes','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1504384308090-c894fdcc538d?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Mars','Telescope','Discovery'],'date'=>'2025-10-29 07:26:00'],
