        ['id'=>10561,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>896,'title'=>'Data Breach: 165 Million landmark Accounts Exposed in Cloud Misconfiguration','exc'=>'The incident highlighted the exposure that came with centralising sensitive data in cloud environments operated by third parties over whose security practices organisations had limited visibility.','body'=>'<p>The situation developed with a speed that left observers struggling to keep pace, as each new development built on the last in ways that underscored the interconnected nature of the forces at work.</p><p>Those with deep expertise in the area described it as a confluence of trends that had each been building independently for years before arriving simultaneously at a point of acute pressure.</p><p>The institutional response was measured, with officials taking care to frame their position in a way that acknowledged the complexity without appearing to minimise the significance of what was unfolding.</p><p>What comes next remains genuinely uncertain, though the structural conditions that produced the current moment show no sign of resolving themselves quickly or easily.</p>','cat'=>'Technology','author'=>'Ravi Patel','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1526374965328-7f61d4dc18c5?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Infrastructure','Vulnerability','Patch'],'date'=>'2023-07-16 09:44:00'],
