        ['id'=>10576,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1430,'title'=>'Cyber Insurance Premiums Rise 79% as Claims Spiral','exc'=>'The incident highlighted the exposure that came with centralising sensitive data in cloud environments operated by third parties over whose security practices organisations had limited visibility.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Technology','author'=>'Nadia Kowalski','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1526374965328-7f61d4dc18c5?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Data Breach','Privacy','Encryption'],'date'=>'2022-12-08 19:51:00'],
