        ['id'=>10712,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2699,'title'=>'twenty% of New Car Sales in controversial Now Electric, Ahead of Target','exc'=>'The expansion of autonomous ride-hailing triggered an immediate political debate about employment displacement, with labour unions arguing that the move required a broader social contract than the company had offered.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Technology','author'=>'Chloe Marsh','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1550751827-4bd374c3f58b?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['EV','Tesla','Battery'],'date'=>'2022-10-26 18:21:00'],
