        ['id'=>10856,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>3177,'title'=>'Michelin Star Restaurant Uses Entirely Local far-reaching Radius Ingredients','exc'=>'Chefs interviewed for the report described a perfect storm of rising food costs, staff shortages, and consumers who had been conditioned by delivery apps to expect restaurant-quality food at supermarket prices.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Lifestyle','author'=>'Aisha Patel','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1484480974693-6ca0a78fb36b?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Sustainability','Waste','Local'],'date'=>'2024-06-02 13:10:00'],
