        ['id'=>10872,'published'=>true,'featured'=>true,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2198,'title'=>'Digital Nomad Visa Issued to 180 Thousand Workers by 166 Nations','exc'=>'Destination managers said they were caught between the economic benefits of visitor spending and the irreversible damage that volumes beyond carrying capacity were causing to the sites themselves.','body'=>'<p>The situation developed with a speed that left observers struggling to keep pace, as each new development built on the last in ways that underscored the interconnected nature of the forces at work.</p><p>Those with deep expertise in the area described it as a confluence of trends that had each been building independently for years before arriving simultaneously at a point of acute pressure.</p><p>The institutional response was measured, with officials taking care to frame their position in a way that acknowledged the complexity without appearing to minimise the significance of what was unfolding.</p><p>What comes next remains genuinely uncertain, though the structural conditions that produced the current moment show no sign of resolving themselves quickly or easily.</p>','cat'=>'Lifestyle','author'=>'Zoe Williams','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506126613408-eca07ce68773?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Adventure','Solo','Nomad'],'date'=>'2024-08-30 05:13:00'],
        ['id'=>10873,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>4943,'title'=>'Leadership Crisis: unexpected% of Managers Feel Ill-Equipped to Manage Hybrid Teams','exc'=>'Employees who chose to leave described a loss of trust in leadership that they said had crystallised around the return mandate but had its roots in a much longer history of mixed messages from the top.','body'=>'<p>Numbers can capture the scale of what occurred but not its texture. Behind the figures were individual stories that defied easy summary and that the official account, necessarily schematic, was unable to convey.</p><p>Researchers who had spent years tracking the subject described a mix of vindication and alarm at how events had unfolded, saying the data had long pointed in this direction but that the pace was faster than even pessimistic scenarios had suggested.</p><p>The policy response drew criticism from those who argued it was too slow, too limited, and too deferential to interests that had contributed to the situation rather than helping to prevent it.</p><p>Future analysis will inevitably focus on the decisions not taken in the years before, and on whether different choices at key junctures would have led to materially different outcomes.</p>','cat'=>'Lifestyle','author'=>'Tariq Farouk','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1512621776951-a57141f6eedf?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Burnout','Wellbeing','Mental Health'],'date'=>'2024-04-03 22:27:00'],
