        ['id'=>11030,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>3227,'title'=>'a hundred and fifty% of Hospital Admissions Linked to Preventable Lifestyle Factors','exc'=>'Public health officials said the figures represented a failure of prevention policy that had been visible for years in the data and that only structural changes to food systems would meaningfully address.','body'=>'<p>When the full account is eventually written, historians will note the particular quality of the moment: the sense among those living through it that something significant was happening, combined with an inability to be certain about precisely what it meant.</p><p>Contemporaries who tried to find precedents for comparison found them only partially useful, because while the surface resemblances were real, the underlying conditions were different enough to make analogies more misleading than illuminating.</p><p>What was not in doubt was that the event had accelerated timelines and concentrated minds in ways that incrementalism alone would not have achieved in the same period.</p><p>The challenge now was to convert that concentrated attention into durable commitments, a challenge that history suggested was substantially harder than the moments of acute focus that preceded it might imply.</p>','cat'=>'Lifestyle','author'=>'Isabella Rossi','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1545205597-3d9d02c29597?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Health','Wellness','Obesity'],'date'=>'2023-11-18 12:01:00'],
        ['id'=>11031,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1340,'title'=>'School Meal Quality Survey Finds 34% of Menus Fail Nutritional Standards','exc'=>'The certification represented a significant regulatory milestone and would, advocates hoped, help close the gap between the environmental cost of conventional production and the alternatives that science now made possible.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Lifestyle','author'=>'Marcus Hayes','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1484480974693-6ca0a78fb36b?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Food','Nutrition','Diet'],'date'=>'2024-07-19 20:08:00'],
