        ['id'=>11140,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>510,'title'=>'a hundred% of Adults in critical Classified as Obese, New Health Survey Finds','exc'=>'The finding added to a growing body of evidence that the environments people lived in, the food they could afford, and the stress they were under mattered at least as much as individual behaviour in determining health outcomes.','body'=>'<p>Few events arrive fully formed. The roots of this one stretched back further than most accounts acknowledged, through a series of decisions, deferred choices, and accumulated pressures that had been visible to specialists for years.</p><p>The immediate trigger was real enough, but veterans of the subject said it should be understood as the proximate rather than the underlying cause of a development that had, in retrospect, an air of inevitability.</p><p>Institutions moved to respond, though the speed and coherence of that response drew mixed assessments from outside observers who questioned whether the frameworks in place were suited to what they were now being asked to manage.</p><p>The longer-term significance will be debated for years, but the immediate effect was to reshape the landscape in ways that all parties involved will need to navigate carefully if the situation is to stabilise.</p>','cat'=>'Lifestyle','author'=>'Isabella Rossi','img'=>'','tags'=>['Health','Wellness','Obesity'],'date'=>'2024-02-24 05:01:00'],
