        ['id'=>11164,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>3399,'title'=>'BNPL Debt Traps fifteen Thousand in Spiral of Revolving Credit','exc'=>'Economists described the savings rate data as a leading indicator of household financial health, saying the decline suggested many families had already exhausted the buffers built up during the pandemic period.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Lifestyle','author'=>'Emma Laurent','img'=>'','tags'=>['Credit','Spending','Cost of Living'],'date'=>'2025-01-31 17:05:00'],
