        ['id'=>11556,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>5145,'title'=>'197 Becomes First significant to Score controversial International Test Centuries','exc'=>'Selectors faced difficult choices as player availability was complicated by the congested international schedule, a problem that cricket administrators had long debated without arriving at a durable solution.','body'=>'<p>Numbers can capture the scale of what occurred but not its texture. Behind the figures were individual stories that defied easy summary and that the official account, necessarily schematic, was unable to convey.</p><p>Researchers who had spent years tracking the subject described a mix of vindication and alarm at how events had unfolded, saying the data had long pointed in this direction but that the pace was faster than even pessimistic scenarios had suggested.</p><p>The policy response drew criticism from those who argued it was too slow, too limited, and too deferential to interests that had contributed to the situation rather than helping to prevent it.</p><p>Future analysis will inevitably focus on the decisions not taken in the years before, and on whether different choices at key junctures would have led to materially different outcomes.</p>','cat'=>'Sports','author'=>'Patrick Durand','img'=>'','tags'=>['Kohli','Stokes','Batting'],'date'=>'2023-06-20 09:51:00'],
        ['id'=>11557,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1068,'title'=>'Davis Cup Reform: 462 Format Changes Divide Tennis Community','exc'=>'Prize money discussions had been ongoing for years and the outcome, while celebrated by advocates, was described by others as long overdue recognition of an inequality that had been visible throughout the sport\'s professional era.','body'=>'<p>Few events arrive fully formed. The roots of this one stretched back further than most accounts acknowledged, through a series of decisions, deferred choices, and accumulated pressures that had been visible to specialists for years.</p><p>The immediate trigger was real enough, but veterans of the subject said it should be understood as the proximate rather than the underlying cause of a development that had, in retrospect, an air of inevitability.</p><p>Institutions moved to respond, though the speed and coherence of that response drew mixed assessments from outside observers who questioned whether the frameworks in place were suited to what they were now being asked to manage.</p><p>The longer-term significance will be debated for years, but the immediate effect was to reshape the landscape in ways that all parties involved will need to navigate carefully if the situation is to stabilise.</p>','cat'=>'Sports','author'=>'Amara Diallo','img'=>'','tags'=>['ATP','WTA','Rankings'],'date'=>'2022-11-16 07:15:00'],
