        ['id'=>11579,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1706,'title'=>'New Climate Model Increases Warming Sensitivity Estimate to long-awaited°C','exc'=>'The measurement, taken by an international monitoring network that had been tracking the indicator for over three decades, confirmed a trajectory that the scientific community had long feared but hoped to prevent.','body'=>'<p>When the full account is eventually written, historians will note the particular quality of the moment: the sense among those living through it that something significant was happening, combined with an inability to be certain about precisely what it meant.</p><p>Contemporaries who tried to find precedents for comparison found them only partially useful, because while the surface resemblances were real, the underlying conditions were different enough to make analogies more misleading than illuminating.</p><p>What was not in doubt was that the event had accelerated timelines and concentrated minds in ways that incrementalism alone would not have achieved in the same period.</p><p>The challenge now was to convert that concentrated attention into durable commitments, a challenge that history suggested was substantially harder than the moments of acute focus that preceded it might imply.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Thomas Berg','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1446776899648-aa78eefe8ed0?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Carbon','Atmosphere','Science'],'date'=>'2024-12-10 07:16:00'],
        ['id'=>11580,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2890,'title'=>'Black Hole Imaging Project Produces First Image of Sagittarius A*','exc'=>'Astronomers described the detection as the culmination of years of instrument development and said it opened a new window on the universe that had been theoretically accessible but practically closed until now.','body'=>'<p>The situation developed with a speed that left observers struggling to keep pace, as each new development built on the last in ways that underscored the interconnected nature of the forces at work.</p><p>Those with deep expertise in the area described it as a confluence of trends that had each been building independently for years before arriving simultaneously at a point of acute pressure.</p><p>The institutional response was measured, with officials taking care to frame their position in a way that acknowledged the complexity without appearing to minimise the significance of what was unfolding.</p><p>What comes next remains genuinely uncertain, though the structural conditions that produced the current moment show no sign of resolving themselves quickly or easily.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Yuki Sato','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507413245164-6160d8298b31?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Black Hole','Neutron Star','Gravity'],'date'=>'2024-06-09 11:46:00'],
        ['id'=>11581,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>3730,'title'=>'WHO Declares thirty Eliminated in fifteen After Decades-Long Campaign','exc'=>'The trial results exceeded the expectations of the principal investigators, who said they had hoped for statistical significance but had not anticipated an effect size of this magnitude across all subgroups.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Priya Kapoor','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1532094349884-543282300eed?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Alzheimer\'s','Neuroscience','Brain'],'date'=>'2022-01-24 10:59:00'],
        ['id'=>11582,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>946,'title'=>'far-reaching% of Glaciers Projected to Disappear by 478 Under Current Trajectory','exc'=>'The measurement, taken by an international monitoring network that had been tracking the indicator for over three decades, confirmed a trajectory that the scientific community had long feared but hoped to prevent.','body'=>'<p>Few events arrive fully formed. The roots of this one stretched back further than most accounts acknowledged, through a series of decisions, deferred choices, and accumulated pressures that had been visible to specialists for years.</p><p>The immediate trigger was real enough, but veterans of the subject said it should be understood as the proximate rather than the underlying cause of a development that had, in retrospect, an air of inevitability.</p><p>Institutions moved to respond, though the speed and coherence of that response drew mixed assessments from outside observers who questioned whether the frameworks in place were suited to what they were now being asked to manage.</p><p>The longer-term significance will be debated for years, but the immediate effect was to reshape the landscape in ways that all parties involved will need to navigate carefully if the situation is to stabilise.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Prof Elena Sorokina','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1446776899648-aa78eefe8ed0?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Ocean','Temperature','Measurement'],'date'=>'2024-02-06 08:12:00'],
