        ['id'=>11647,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>4336,'title'=>'Lab-Grown Cornea Restores Sight to 375 Blind Patients','exc'=>'Regulators faced pressure to accelerate approval pathways for a therapy that patient advocacy groups said represented the first genuine breakthrough in the field in more than a decade.','body'=>'<p>Few events arrive fully formed. The roots of this one stretched back further than most accounts acknowledged, through a series of decisions, deferred choices, and accumulated pressures that had been visible to specialists for years.</p><p>The immediate trigger was real enough, but veterans of the subject said it should be understood as the proximate rather than the underlying cause of a development that had, in retrospect, an air of inevitability.</p><p>Institutions moved to respond, though the speed and coherence of that response drew mixed assessments from outside observers who questioned whether the frameworks in place were suited to what they were now being asked to manage.</p><p>The longer-term significance will be debated for years, but the immediate effect was to reshape the landscape in ways that all parties involved will need to navigate carefully if the situation is to stabilise.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Marcus Levin','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1532094349884-543282300eed?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Medicine','Cancer','Trial'],'date'=>'2024-02-15 19:55:00'],
        ['id'=>11648,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>527,'title'=>'Antarctic Glacier Retreat Accelerates, Raising Sea Level Risk','exc'=>'The researchers described the finding as deeply troubling, noting that it implied a remaining budget for emissions far smaller than the figures that had been used to frame current policy discussions.','body'=>'<p>Numbers can capture the scale of what occurred but not its texture. Behind the figures were individual stories that defied easy summary and that the official account, necessarily schematic, was unable to convey.</p><p>Researchers who had spent years tracking the subject described a mix of vindication and alarm at how events had unfolded, saying the data had long pointed in this direction but that the pace was faster than even pessimistic scenarios had suggested.</p><p>The policy response drew criticism from those who argued it was too slow, too limited, and too deferential to interests that had contributed to the situation rather than helping to prevent it.</p><p>Future analysis will inevitably focus on the decisions not taken in the years before, and on whether different choices at key junctures would have led to materially different outcomes.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Sarah Mitchell','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1446776899648-aa78eefe8ed0?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Climate','Emissions','IPCC'],'date'=>'2025-01-16 15:07:00'],
        ['id'=>11649,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>735,'title'=>'Comet five Contains Complex Organic Molecules Including fifty Precursors','exc'=>'The discovery warranted follow-up observation with multiple independent instruments, the team said, before any firm conclusions about its significance could be drawn from what remained, at this stage, a statistical signal.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Prof James Okonkwo','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507413245164-6160d8298b31?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Space','Webb','Astronomy'],'date'=>'2024-04-05 19:47:00'],
