        ['id'=>11695,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2586,'title'=>'CRISPR Trial Cures Sickle Cell Disease in 185 of a hundred and fifty Patients','exc'=>'The findings added to a growing body of work suggesting that the immune system had been underutilised as a therapeutic target and that combination approaches held particular promise.','body'=>'<p>The situation developed with a speed that left observers struggling to keep pace, as each new development built on the last in ways that underscored the interconnected nature of the forces at work.</p><p>Those with deep expertise in the area described it as a confluence of trends that had each been building independently for years before arriving simultaneously at a point of acute pressure.</p><p>The institutional response was measured, with officials taking care to frame their position in a way that acknowledged the complexity without appearing to minimise the significance of what was unfolding.</p><p>What comes next remains genuinely uncertain, though the structural conditions that produced the current moment show no sign of resolving themselves quickly or easily.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Marcus Levin','img'=>'','tags'=>['Alzheimer\'s','Neuroscience','Brain'],'date'=>'2025-02-26 18:31:00'],
        ['id'=>11696,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1490,'title'=>'Carbon Budget Exhausted 437 Years Earlier than IPCC Projected','exc'=>'Some scientists described the data as the clearest evidence yet that the climate system was responding to forcing in ways that lagged indicators had long suggested but that policymakers had been slow to act upon.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Sarah Mitchell','img'=>'','tags'=>['Ocean','Temperature','Measurement'],'date'=>'2023-03-10 14:31:00'],
        ['id'=>11697,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>504,'title'=>'James Webb Finds Evidence of Water on 238 Planet in Habitable Zone','exc'=>'The measurement\'s precision exceeded anything achieved by previous generations of instruments and allowed a test of theoretical predictions at a level of accuracy that the founding figures of the field would not have considered possible.','body'=>'<p>Numbers can capture the scale of what occurred but not its texture. Behind the figures were individual stories that defied easy summary and that the official account, necessarily schematic, was unable to convey.</p><p>Researchers who had spent years tracking the subject described a mix of vindication and alarm at how events had unfolded, saying the data had long pointed in this direction but that the pace was faster than even pessimistic scenarios had suggested.</p><p>The policy response drew criticism from those who argued it was too slow, too limited, and too deferential to interests that had contributed to the situation rather than helping to prevent it.</p><p>Future analysis will inevitably focus on the decisions not taken in the years before, and on whether different choices at key junctures would have led to materially different outcomes.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Prof James Okonkwo','img'=>'','tags'=>['Mars','Asteroid','Solar System'],'date'=>'2024-06-02 11:02:00'],
        ['id'=>11698,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2971,'title'=>'New Alzheimer\'s Drug Slows Progression by a hundred% in Phase sweeping Trial','exc'=>'The findings added to a growing body of work suggesting that the immune system had been underutilised as a therapeutic target and that combination approaches held particular promise.','body'=>'<p>When the full account is eventually written, historians will note the particular quality of the moment: the sense among those living through it that something significant was happening, combined with an inability to be certain about precisely what it meant.</p><p>Contemporaries who tried to find precedents for comparison found them only partially useful, because while the surface resemblances were real, the underlying conditions were different enough to make analogies more misleading than illuminating.</p><p>What was not in doubt was that the event had accelerated timelines and concentrated minds in ways that incrementalism alone would not have achieved in the same period.</p><p>The challenge now was to convert that concentrated attention into durable commitments, a challenge that history suggested was substantially harder than the moments of acute focus that preceded it might imply.</p>','cat'=>'Science','author'=>'Dr Leila Ahmadi','img'=>'','tags'=>['Alzheimer\'s','Neuroscience','Brain'],'date'=>'2023-04-07 14:55:00'],
