        ['id'=>11766,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>2671,'title'=>'Harris Nomination Makes History as First two hundred to Lead Major Party Ticket','exc'=>'The decision was defended by administration officials as legally sound and within executive authority, while opponents mounted an immediate legal challenge that was expected to reach the Supreme Court.','body'=>'<p>The situation developed with a speed that left observers struggling to keep pace, as each new development built on the last in ways that underscored the interconnected nature of the forces at work.</p><p>Those with deep expertise in the area described it as a confluence of trends that had each been building independently for years before arriving simultaneously at a point of acute pressure.</p><p>The institutional response was measured, with officials taking care to frame their position in a way that acknowledged the complexity without appearing to minimise the significance of what was unfolding.</p><p>What comes next remains genuinely uncertain, though the structural conditions that produced the current moment show no sign of resolving themselves quickly or easily.</p>','cat'=>'Politics','author'=>'Viktor Havel','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1529107386315-e1a2ed48a620?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Supreme Court','Constitution','Rights'],'date'=>'2025-01-19 14:07:00'],
        ['id'=>11767,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>1531,'title'=>'Scottish Independence Vote Called After fifteen SNP Electoral Victory','exc'=>'Coalition arithmetic proved intractable, with parties that had governed together for years unable to agree on the terms of a new relationship following an election that had reshuffled their relative positions.','body'=>'<p>When the full account is eventually written, historians will note the particular quality of the moment: the sense among those living through it that something significant was happening, combined with an inability to be certain about precisely what it meant.</p><p>Contemporaries who tried to find precedents for comparison found them only partially useful, because while the surface resemblances were real, the underlying conditions were different enough to make analogies more misleading than illuminating.</p><p>What was not in doubt was that the event had accelerated timelines and concentrated minds in ways that incrementalism alone would not have achieved in the same period.</p><p>The challenge now was to convert that concentrated attention into durable commitments, a challenge that history suggested was substantially harder than the moments of acute focus that preceded it might imply.</p>','cat'=>'Politics','author'=>'Siobhan Murray','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1573804633927-bfcbcd909acd?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Brexit','Scotland','Sovereignty'],'date'=>'2023-11-04 14:40:00'],
        ['id'=>11768,'published'=>true,'featured'=>false,'breaking'=>false,'views'=>231,'title'=>'Department of Justice Sues landmark States Over major Legislation','exc'=>'The decision was defended by administration officials as legally sound and within executive authority, while opponents mounted an immediate legal challenge that was expected to reach the Supreme Court.','body'=>'<p>The announcement was received with a range of reactions that reflected genuinely different assessments of the evidence, the stakes, and the appropriate weight to give competing considerations.</p><p>Supporters argued that the decision represented a rational response to conditions that could not be indefinitely ignored, while critics maintained that the approach risked unintended consequences that had not been adequately modelled.</p><p>Both positions had merit, and the honest answer was that the situation involved real trade-offs between values and interests that did not admit of a perfect resolution — only better or worse choices among imperfect options.</p><p>The debate continued in the days that followed, with new information and perspectives adding detail to a picture that remained incomplete and in certain key respects contested.</p>','cat'=>'Politics','author'=>'Jonathan Clarke','img'=>'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1529107386315-e1a2ed48a620?w=800&q=80','tags'=>['Supreme Court','Constitution','Rights'],'date'=>'2023-08-21 20:23:00'],
